-- title:
--   Reduction mod ℓ commutes with the Fricke involution
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$, let $\ell$ be a prime not dividing $N$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of a fixed algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $\mathbb Q$ which lies over $\ell$ in the sense that $\ell$, viewed in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is a nonunit of $A$; write $k$ for the residue field of $A$. On the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-side, `modularFunctionFieldBar N` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the subfield `modularFunctionFieldFull N` of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions attached to $N$, and `JZero N` is its group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of degree-zero divisor classes modulo principal ones. On the $k$-side, `modularFunctionFieldFullC k N` is the intermediate field of $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}_d(j)$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, where $j$ denotes the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNum}$ over $k$ and $\mathrm{qExpand}_d$ substitutes $q\mapsto q^d$. Let $\tau$ be any $k$-algebra automorphism of `modularFunctionFieldFullC k N` such that $\tau(\mathrm{qExpand}_a(j)) = \mathrm{qExpand}_b(j)$ whenever $ab = N$ with $a,b$ nonzero. Then for every $z\in$ `JZero N`, the reduction map `reductionModL A N` (reduction of degree-zero divisor classes along the residue map of $A$) satisfies $\mathrm{red}_A(w_N\cdot z) = \tau\cdot \mathrm{red}_A(z)$, where $w_N$ is `frickeInvolutionBar N`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the chosen Fricke automorphism of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, and automorphisms act on $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ by transport of divisor classes.
--
--   This is the classical compatibility, going back to Deuring and Igusa, of the reduction of $X_0(N)$ at a prime $\ell$ of good reduction with the Fricke (Atkin–Lehner) involution $w_N$: the involution is defined over $\mathbb Z[1/N]$ and hence commutes with specialisation of divisor classes on the Jacobian. It is used, in combination with the compatibility of reduction with Hecke correspondences, to identify $\bar U_p$ with $-\bar w_p$ on the Jacobian of the special fibre of $X_0(p)$, the form in which it enters [`ModularCurve.heckePic0Fibre_eq_neg_fricke_smul_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.heckePic0Fibre_eq_neg_fricke_smul_of_prime).
-- source:
